Z||000005||BN Boomer||06-30-2000||03:36 PM||||1142 miles in 32 hours should be no problem. That's just under 36mph average speed, even a Fiero should be able to maintain that.<P>While traveling to temporary work assignments, I've driven my Suburban 2400 miles from Seattle, WA to Temple, TX, in 40 hours and 1620 miles from Seattle to Willmar, MN in 24 hrs. Not that I'd make a habit of doing this, but it wasn't any big deal. A 42 gallon gas tank and the fact that there wasn't a speed limit in Montana during these trips helped, too.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by BN Boomer (edited 06-30-2000).]||||reg||1
